  "Bug_Title": "UseNotifyAllInsteadOfNotify",
  "Bug_Details": "Thread.notify() awakens a thread monitoring the object. If more than one thread is monitoring, then only\none is chosen.  The thread chosen is arbitrary; thus it's usually safer to call notifyAll() instead.",
  "Bug_Explanation": "The bug is embedded in the `doSomething` method, where the `lock.notify()` method is used instead of `lock.notifyAll()`. This line is marked with the comment `// BUG: UseNotifyAllInsteadOfNotify`.",
